  "independent_source_findings": [
    "The first successful drain header, first coordinator session and first observations remain immutable.",
    "All 174 owned page pointers and physical addresses, consumer/maps/bootstrap/root descriptor identities are captured before first PWRGATE and compared before/after the second cycle.",
    "Second intent is consumed before hardware and independently seals the copied receive worker without rewriting first seal/session-failed evidence; fresh strict OFF and suspended held0/usage0/error0 admission precede one separately owned PM resume_and_get.",
    "Fresh ACTIVE and held1/usage1/error0 precede ASC/mailbox access; four valid CTRL44/STATUS48/RX114/TX110 operands require START clear, exact0x6a, RX empty and TX available before and after separate paired ON.",
    "The sole START write reads CTRL44 again immediately before OR0x10 and refuses invalid/reasserted START; readback is required.",
    "Separate bounded protocol journal records every removed frame before interpretation; EP0 HELLO12/12 precedes exact maps base0/bitmap3/nonfinal then base1/bitmap3/final. Full six-bit base is extracted, shape refusal precedes ACK, and successful final ACK precedes map admission.",
    "Before the sole second0x202, reserve ACK journal capacity and freshly require four valid operands, START set, RX empty, TX available and held1/usage1/ACTIVE/error0 with second coordinator ON complete.",
    "Own EP0 type7/low8{1,2} ACK and fresh RX empty precede native idle, fresh checked clear0x10 then clear0x20, separate paired OFF, one second PM put and strict physical OFF/accounting.",
    "After consumed second put only PMGR/software and retained DRAM identity observations remain; no ASC, SGX, mailbox, PMP or PMC access is added.",
    "Complete is set only after final immutable first-evidence and retained-identity checks; every outcome retains all resources and seals additional controls. Retained diagnostics use the frozen no-ASC-after-first-OFF gate.",
    "No new root/context publication, app endpoint start, AP-on, INIT220, DATA copy, reset vector, queue/counter reset, unmap or allocation retirement is introduced."
  ],
